  "body": " Situation B: Pumpkin Launch   At a fall festival, a pumpkin is fired straight up from an air cannon set on a bluff above Lake Michigan. The height of the pumpkin in feet above the surface of the lake, seconds after it is fired, is given by   The graph of is shown below. The horizontal intercepts, vertical intercept, and vertex all occur at integer coordinates.   A downward opening parabola showing height in feet against time in seconds, with horizontal intercepts at negative one and seven, vertical intercept at one hundred twelve, and vertex at three comma two hundred fifty-six.   A parabola opening downward on a coordinate grid with time on the horizontal axis and height on the vertical axis. The curve crosses the horizontal axis at the points negative one comma zero and seven comma zero, crosses the vertical axis at zero comma one hundred twelve, and reaches its highest point at three comma two hundred fifty-six.        Write in factored form and in vertex form. Show the work that produces each one.    Factor out : . Two numbers that multiply to and add to are and , so .  The vertex sits halfway between the zeros: . Then , so . Check at : , matching the vertical intercept.      Identify the vertical intercept. What does it mean in this situation?    The vertical intercept is . At , the moment the cannon fires, the pumpkin is feet above the surface of the lake. That is the height of the bluff where the cannon is set up.      Identify the horizontal intercepts. Explain what each one means and which one describes the pumpkin.    The horizontal intercepts are and , the times when the height equals feet, meaning the pumpkin is at the surface of the lake.  The pumpkin splashes into the lake seconds after it is fired, so is the meaningful intercept. The intercept is one second before the cannon fired and has no meaning in this situation. Both are solutions of , but only one of them is part of the story.      Identify the vertex. What does it mean in this situation?    The vertex is . Because the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward and the vertex is the maximum. The pumpkin reaches its greatest height, feet above the lake, seconds after being fired. It is rising before that moment and falling after it.      Find . What does this value tell you about the pumpkin?    Using factored form, feet. (General form agrees: .)  Five seconds after the cannon fires, the pumpkin is feet above the lake. Since comes after the vertex at , the pumpkin is falling at that moment. It is still well above the water, since it does not land until .      Find all values of for which . Show your algebraic steps and explain what your answers mean.    Set the general form equal to : . Subtract to get . Divide by to get , which factors as . The solutions are and .  The pumpkin is feet above the lake at seconds while rising and again at seconds while falling. Both are meaningful, since both happen between the launch and the splash. Reading between them, the pumpkin is higher than feet for the whole interval .      What values of make sense as inputs in this situation? Explain how you decided.    The inputs that make sense are , from the moment the cannon fires until the pumpkin hits the water.  Times before are not described by the model, and times after produce negative outputs, which would put the pumpkin below the surface of the lake. For instance, , and a height of feet is not something this situation can produce.      A festival organizer claims the pumpkin passed feet above the lake. Use both the graph and the algebra to explain why that cannot be true.    On the graph, the highest point on the curve is the vertex at a height of feet. A horizontal line at would sit entirely above the parabola and never touch it, so there is no time when the height equals feet.  Algebraically, setting gives . Dividing by gives , and the discriminant is . A negative discriminant means there are no real solutions, which is the algebra's way of saying the same thing the graph says: the pumpkin never gets that high.    "
